kdown","lines":343,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10007,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-crm/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":772,"executable":false,"size_bytes":18498,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-inventory/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":863,"executable":false,"size_bytes":22948,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-mail/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":534,"executable":false,"size_bytes":16052,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-people/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":377,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10143,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-projects/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":532,"executable":false,"size_bytes":13303,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoho-recruit/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":533,"executable":false,"size_bytes":14698,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoom-admin/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":496,"executable":false,"size_bytes":14841,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/zoom/README.md","type":"markdown","lines":459,"executable":false,"size_bytes":11065,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3aaec223bfe3487192e4d8f9061ad6b1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/acuity-scheduling/README.md","start_line":38,"end_line":86},"finding":null,"explanation":"The appointments listing example and response include names, phone numbers, email addresses, and scheduling details, but the markdown does not warn users that these requests may reveal sensitive personal data. Under the markdown-file criteria, skills should disclose behaviors that could affect user privacy.","remediation":"Add a short warning near the Appointments API section stating that appointment endpoints may expose personal client data and should only be queried when the user intends to access that information and is authorized to do so.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/acuity-scheduling/README.md","start_line":38,"end_line":86}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d53a441cfcf64d2c9c4a1f56d96ea1fd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"references/acuity-scheduling/README.md","start_line":277,"end_line":304},"finding":null,"explanation":"The Clients API examples show retrieval of names, email addresses, phone numbers, and notes, but there is no accompanying warning about handling client records or privacy implications. For markdown files, omission of warnings about user-data-affecting behavior is in scope.","remediation":"Add a warning in the Clients API section that listing clients returns sensitive personal information and should be used only with clear user intent and appropriate authorization.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/acuity-scheduling/README.md","start_line":277,"end_line":304}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9befd6f691414a529c17c3bb1541cb96","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/calendly/README.md","start_line":530,"end_line":538},"finding":null,"explanation":"The delete webhook example performs a persistent configuration change that can silently disable event delivery to an external destination, but the section lacks the same explicit confirmation and warning language used for webhook creation. In this skill, webhook subscriptions forward future scheduling events containing personal data, so deleting one can break integrations, audit flows, or compliance-related processing if executed on ambiguous or unverified user intent.","remediation":"Add an explicit warning before the deletion example stating that deleting a webhook stops future event forwarding and requires clear user confirmation of the exact subscription to remove. Instruct the agent to list existing webhook subscriptions first, identify the target by destination URL and scope, and confirm the user wants that specific persistent forwarding path disabled before issuing DELETE.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/calendly/README.md","start_line":530,"end_line":538}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9eb5ab6623134c0994191b3c547f248f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.83,"location":{"file":"references/getresponse/README.md","start_line":173,"end_line":426},"finding":null,"explanation":"Although L005 provides a general confirmation requirement for write operations, this README does not specifically warn that several documented actions can send communications to recipients or upload contact data, which can affect user privacy and have irreversible external effects. For markdown files, the skill description should clearly disclose behaviors that could affect user data, privacy, or system integrity.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings near the relevant sections that sending newsletters, transactional emails, and SMS can contact real recipients, and that imports upload contact personal data. Instruct users to verify recipients, schedule, consent, and payload contents before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/getresponse/README.md","start_line":173,"end_line":426}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-084a4da374e848e6a4e3ad0397eaebb3","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":245,"end_line":251},"finding":null,"explanation":"The permanently delete member operation is materially riskier than a normal archive/delete because it irreversibly removes a contact and can affect compliance records, recovery options, and customer data integrity. Although the file has a general write-confirmation policy, this specific endpoint lacks an explicit, local warning about irreversibility, making it easier for an agent or user to treat it like a routine write and execute destructive action without adequate confirmation.","remediation":"Add a prominent endpoint-specific warning stating that this action permanently and irreversibly deletes the member, may have compliance or auditing consequences, and requires explicit user confirmation naming the target list and member. Require a two-step confirmation for irreversible deletions and prefer documenting the safer archive/delete endpoint first.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":245,"end_line":251}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-54eb26c9740a47ddbd96f9eaffb2762f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":512,"end_line":522},"finding":null,"explanation":"Scheduling a campaign is not just a metadata update; it causes future real email delivery to a potentially large audience and can be easy to overlook because the send occurs later. Unlike the adjacent send operation, this section lacks a strong warning to verify campaign identity, recipient scope, send time, and explicit approval, increasing the chance of accidental mass outbound email.","remediation":"Add a warning comparable to the send endpoint that clearly states scheduling will result in real future delivery to the campaign audience. Instruct the agent to present campaign name, subject, sender, recipient count, scheduled time/time zone, and obtain explicit confirmation before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":512,"end_line":522}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0dd5dfacb8f54de38b25b2b99208b9ee","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":615,"end_line":621},"finding":null,"explanation":"Starting an automation activates outbound email workflows that may immediately or subsequently send messages to many recipients based on existing triggers and queue state. Without an explicit warning, an agent may underestimate this as a harmless state toggle rather than a potentially broad email-sending action with reputational and compliance consequences.","remediation":"Document this endpoint with a clear warning that starting an automation can trigger real outbound emails and should only occur after explicit user confirmation. Require verification of the workflow name, target audience/trigger scope, current status, and expected sending behavior before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":615,"end_line":621}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-dd95569925304252aac1f268436085ef","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":639,"end_line":651},"finding":null,"explanation":"Queueing a subscriber into an automation can trigger real automated email sends to a specific individual, potentially without their current consent context being rechecked. The lack of a local warning obscures that this is an externally impactful action, not a benign queue-management step, and can lead to unauthorized or accidental customer contact.","remediation":"Add an endpoint-specific warning that this action may immediately enroll the named subscriber into a live email workflow and trigger outbound messages. Require explicit confirmation of the workflow, email step, subscriber identity, and consent/eligibility before allowing execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/mailchimp/README.md","start_line":639,"end_line":651}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-913e0366918745739bcde05198ff1670","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"references/posthog/README.md","start_line":10,"end_line":47},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README claims gateway-injected credentials are never carried in requests, but the included example response exposes a PostHog project `api_token` (`phc_XXX`). Even if redacted in the example, documenting and surfacing credential-bearing fields without stronger warnings can normalize handling secrets in responses and may lead agents or users to display, log, or forward live tokens from real API results.","remediation":"Update the documentation to explicitly warn that some read endpoints may return sensitive fields such as project API tokens, and instruct agents to redact or omit them from outputs. Replace the example with a sanitized response that removes the `api_token` field entirely, and add guidance to avoid logging or transferring returned credentials unless strictly required and explicitly approved.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/posthog/README.md","start_line":10,"end_line":47}]},{"id":"SDI-1","finding_id":"finding-ea3950501bde4b7db3da9ab4ac0eb9f2","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/sunsama-mcp/schemas/delete_email_thread.json","start_line":2,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest frames this skill primarily as a gateway for calling connected third-party APIs, with read/list as the default and writes requiring explicit user confirmation. This schema exposes a permanently destructive mailbox operation, which goes beyond the manifest's baseline expectation of routine API reads and introduces a higher-risk behavior that should be tightly constrained.","remediation":"Ensure the manifest clearly and prominently discloses destructive mailbox-deletion capabilities, or restrict this tool to contexts with explicit user confirmation and additional policy gating. If this capability is intended, document it as a high-risk write operation in the skill's declared scope.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/sunsama-mcp/schemas/delete_email_thread.json","start_line":2,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-635293b4a8e844ea835f2ccebd423cbd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/telegram/README.md","start_line":96,"end_line":245},"finding":null,"explanation":"The examples for sendMessage/sendPhoto/sendDocument/sendVideo/sendAudio/sendLocation/sendContact/sendPoll/sendDice show outbound delivery actions without consistently warning that user-provided or retrieved content will be disclosed into a Telegram chat visible to that chat’s members. In this skill, write operations already require explicit confirmation, but missing per-operation disclosure guidance increases the chance an agent forwards sensitive data, uploads third-party content, or messages the wrong audience without clearly informing the user of the privacy consequence.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings before outbound messaging/media examples stating that the content will be sent to the specified chat and become visible to its participants, and require confirmation of the exact chat_id/recipient and message/media content. For forwarding-style or content-bearing actions, instruct agents not to source recipients or payloads from untrusted message content and to summarize the disclosure effect before execution.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/telegram/README.md","start_line":96,"end_line":245}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d05f4167923e45bc96b409b58c3f790f","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"references/twilio/README.md","start_line":453,"end_line":463},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README documents creating a Twilio Address resource using real-world street, city, postal code, and customer name fields, but unlike other sensitive or destructive operations it provides no privacy or confirmation warning. In this skill context, that omission increases the chance an agent will collect, transmit, or echo personally identifiable information to a live third-party account without adequate minimization or explicit user confirmation.","remediation":"Add a clear safety note before the Create Address example stating that address and customer-name fields are sensitive personal/business data, should only be sent for a user-requested purpose, should be minimized to the required fields, and must not be displayed or retained beyond the task. Require explicit user confirmation before creating or updating address records, similar to other write operations in the file.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/twilio/README.md","start_line":453,"end_line":463}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-2d983261d0d14778b41a14132c619a5e","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"references/unbounce/README.md","start_line":281,"end_line":313},"finding":null,"explanation":"The README exposes read endpoints for lead records that contain third-party personal data such as name, email, phone number, and submitter IP, but it does not pair those read operations with handling guidance comparable to the write-path warning. That omission increases the chance an agent will retrieve, echo, summarize too specifically, or further process personal data without minimization or redisclosure safeguards, especially because lead reads are framed as ordinary list/get calls.","remediation":"Add an explicit privacy warning on lead retrieval endpoints (`List Page Leads` and `Get Lead`) requiring user confirmation that they are authorized to access the data, instruct the agent to minimize fields returned and avoid unnecessary bulk listing, and prohibit echoing raw personal data back unless strictly necessary. Also document safe defaults such as summarizing results, redacting IP/contact fields when possible, and requiring extra caution before exporting, copying, or using retrieved leads in other apps.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/unbounce/README.md","start_line":281,"end_line":313}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d20d0593c2e14eeb8e85ad4e7f5af9b7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"LOW","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"references/telegram/README.md","start_line":398,"end_line":454},"finding":null,"explanation":"The command and profile mutation examples (setMyCommands, deleteMyCommands, setMyDescription, setMyName) omit warnings that these changes persist beyond the current session and alter the bot’s public behavior or presentation for all users interacting with it. While lower impact than data exfiltration, this can still cause unauthorized or accidental operational changes, confusion, or reputational harm if an agent performs these writes without clearly communicating their persistent effect.","remediation":"Prepend these mutation sections with warnings that the action persistently changes bot configuration visible to users until changed again. Require explicit confirmation of the exact new commands/name/description, and recommend checking current settings first so the user understands what will be replaced or removed.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/telegram/README.md","start_line":398,"end_line":454}]}],"suppressed_count":0,"suppressed":[],"metadata":{"has_executable_scripts":false,"skillspector_version":"2.11.2","llm_requested":true,"llm_available":true,"meta_analysis_applied":true,"inference_usage":[{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":7496,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":7510},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":6407,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":6421},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":3678,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":3692},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","usage_source":"provider_response","prompt_tokens":4080,"completion_tokens":14,"cached_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":4094},{"node":"semantic_developer_intent","request_kind":"structured_output","provider":"openai","model":"gpt-5.4-2026-03-05","model_source":"provider_response","